{"title":"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/f/53f12ec5ee4a2e5304810da76fbb60e0d3cf46c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> be an integer. Consider an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/f/93f761f7fc79f2bec21a2f31c896840d6f36cdc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\times n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> chessboard consisting of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> unit squares. A configuration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rooks on this board is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/2743e416e03960344413ed981f3bbdd9675a4f54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{peaceful}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> if every row and every column contains exactly one rook. Find the greatest positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that, for each peaceful configuration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rooks, there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/e/97e11746bde904a399f341e9c7ee8f328c526c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\times k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> square which does not contain a rook on any of its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> squares.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/7/227a34396e45a5c4763c260a048a611ac83c2b7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\lceil \\sqrt{n}\\rceil  - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/1699e689947bc3246c9b3c9ca648e2d85ea6cfde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil n\\rceil$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"19\" /> is the ceiling function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />; i.e., the least integer greater than or equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/4/5c4e098181dd9dd99b62f8292eedc4b5052b98f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lceil n\\rceil  &lt; n + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>First, we shall show that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d38f82f48ef9e81c04d49354293305b0067afc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\times n$\" width=\"43\" height=\"9\" /> chessboard with a peaceful configuration of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> rooks contains a valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3eae791493a49e3c1653ae6b9c861e354c7d03d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\times k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> square. Consider firstly the rook <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on the top row of the board. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/6/7b69542b4470fc340f255ae145f3fb07ab2352dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />, there exists a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> consecutive columns, one of which contains rook <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f5e3b588dc7c81e3c7dde4e47f9146e434b8a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n - k + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3eae791493a49e3c1653ae6b9c861e354c7d03d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\times k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> squares in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Of them, only one contains the rook <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on one of its squares. Furthermore, each of the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/c/efce61aab04f52f5d37708f357df021c8baa7434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k - 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" /> rooks in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> can only make up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3eae791493a49e3c1653ae6b9c861e354c7d03d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\times k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> squares have it on one of its squares. Therefore, because\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/c/53c18219ff1bac70e03a1a0804ed76d0db7c8ec6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n - k + 1 = n - \\lceil \\sqrt{n}\\rceil  + 2 &gt; n - \\sqrt{n} + 1 = \\sqrt{n} (\\sqrt{n} - 1) + 1 &gt; (\\lceil \\sqrt{n}\\rceil  - 1) (\\lceil \\sqrt{n}\\rceil  - 2) + 1 = k(k - 1) + 1,\\]\" width=\"723\" height=\"20\" />\nby the Pigeonhole Principle there exists a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3eae791493a49e3c1653ae6b9c861e354c7d03d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\times k$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> square in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> not covered by any rook in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Clearly, that square cannot be covered by any rook outside of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and so it is a valid choice.\n</p><p>It remains to show that there exists a chessboard without a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0a48c2a3dbc5cbc19e723744072944f3496c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1) \\times (k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> square. Indeed, such a board exists. First, place a rook at the upper-left corner of the board. Next, place a rook 1 space to the right and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cba1efe0450bd8158d00008780f2ad6b1dba387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> spaces down of the first rook. Then, place a rook 1 space to the right and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/b/9cba1efe0450bd8158d00008780f2ad6b1dba387.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> spaces down of the second rook, and so on, until the placement of a new rook will be under the lower boundary of the board. In that case, place a rook in the same unoccupied column and in the first unoccupied row, and continue placement of subsequent rooks. This arrangement of rooks is clearly peaceful, and because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/23931f8026e5b284aff597d7dde4d1e494d5353c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1)^2 &gt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"19\" /> it has the property that any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/0/5c0a48c2a3dbc5cbc19e723744072944f3496c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k+1) \\times (k+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"18\" /> square in the board will be occupied by at least one rook, completing the proof.\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO\" title=\"2014 IMO\">2014 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2014 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017033853\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 242/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1238/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7055/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.938      1 -total\n 58.40%    8.140      1 Template:IMO_box\n 40.65%    5.666      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13389:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017033853 and revision id 99210. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}